<!-- Airhub vs Holafly Comparison Content -->
<div class="content-section">

  {% set airhubPrimary = providerA.codes | findCode(providerA.primaryCode) %}
  {% set airhubBest = providerA.codes | bestValidCode %}
  {% set holaflyPrimary = providerB.codes | findCode(providerB.primaryCode) %}

  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
    <p>
      Pick <strong>Airhub</strong> if you know roughly how much data you'll use and want to pay as little as possible per gigabyte, plus get SMS and a local number bundled in. Pick <strong>Holafly</strong> if you'd rather pay a flat rate and never look at a data meter again. They're not really competing on the same axis: Airhub is a cheap, GB-metered plan with a couple of extras; Holafly is an unlimited flat-rate plan with a higher day-rate.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The Core Difference: Cheap Per-GB Bundles vs. Unlimited Flat Rate</h2>
  <p>
    Airhub sells multi-gigabyte blocks (3GB, 4GB) instead of single-day or single-GB units, and in cheaper destinations that lands at genuinely low per-GB prices: Thailand at $0.85 for 1GB and Japan at $1.55 for 1GB. Holafly skips the GB question entirely and charges a flat daily (or monthly) rate for unlimited data, no matter how much you actually use. If you can estimate your data use and want to pay less, Airhub wins on price. If you can't, or you'd rather not think about it, Holafly's flat rate removes the risk of running out mid-trip.
  </p>
  <p>
    Airhub also bundles SMS and, in many destinations, a local phone number in with the data, which most GB-priced competitors don't do. Holafly's plans are data-only. Neither provider includes voice calls, so neither replaces a real phone number if you need to make or receive calls.
  </p>

  <h2>Price Snapshot (before any code)</h2>
  <div class="content-box">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Destination</th>
          <th>Airhub</th>
          <th>Holafly</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Thailand</td><td>$0.85 (1GB)</td><td>$1.99/day (unlimited)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Japan</td><td>$1.55 (1GB)</td><td>$1.99/day (unlimited)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>United States</td><td>$2.82 (3GB)</td><td>$1.99/day (unlimited)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Europe regional</td><td>$4.50 (4GB)</td><td>$1.99/day (unlimited)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="content-note">Airhub's price is per data bundle; Holafly's is per day of unlimited use. They're not directly comparable numbers: a short trip using well under the bundle size would likely cost less on Airhub, while a trip with heavy streaming or navigation would likely cost less (or at least be less stressful) on Holafly.</p>
  </div>

